<h1>6. System Scope &amp; Major Components</h1>
<h2>6.1 In-scope capabilities</h2><ul><li>Structured hospital blood requests and status history.</li><li>Donor profile and eligibility state, donation records and camp participation.</li><li>Blood-bank locations, inventory lots, expiry-aware stock proposals, reservations and dispatch audit.</li><li>Camp lifecycle, capacity/slots, bookings, roster and attendance.</li><li>Administrator triage, hospital verification, inventory management and human review of agent workflow proposals.</li><li>Optional server-side Firebase push delivery and local logging-provider mode.</li></ul>
<h2>6.2 Out-of-scope clinical authority</h2><p>LifeLink is a coordination prototype. It does not perform laboratory screening, crossmatch testing, patient diagnosis, transfusion prescribing, donor medical assessment or clinical prioritization. Compatibility/eligibility rules in code are educational business logic requiring review by qualified local transfusion professionals before any operational use. It does not replace NBTS systems or claim interoperability with NBTS without formal agreement.</p>
