<h1>18. Agentic AI Evaluation</h1>$agentEvalBody
<h2>18.1 Acceptance evidence matrix</h2><table><tr><th>Acceptance property</th><th>Assertion/evidence</th><th>Unsafe result handling</th></tr><tr><td>Structured objective and plan</td><td>Schema-valid plan has request facts, bounded steps and supported task types.</td><td>Reject malformed plan; deterministic planner fallback or safe failure.</td></tr><tr><td>Distinct delegation</td><td>Persisted graph shows coordinator, analysis, dispatch and validation steps with distinct outputs.</td><td>Missing/duplicated agent participation fails scenario assertion.</td></tr><tr><td>Allow-listed tool use</td><td>Tool call name and argument schema match the reviewed allow-list.</td><td>Unknown tool or invalid argument is rejected; no execution.</td></tr><tr><td>Business-rule validation</td><td>Compatibility, expiry, stock quantity and shortage outcomes match deterministic oracle.</td><td>Unsupported proposal escalates or fails safely.</td></tr><tr><td>Human approval</td><td>Critical dispatch/broadcast proposal remains pending until authorized administrator decision.</td><td>Reject direct execution, unauthorized decision and duplicate side effect.</td></tr><tr><td>Prompt injection / resilience</td><td>Golden cases test instruction attacks, malformed model response, timeout and bounded retry.</td><td>Model cannot widen its tool/permission scope; safe failure is recorded.</td></tr></table>
<p>Use rule-based assertions, versioned schemas, golden scenarios and human domain review; an LLM judge may only supplement these checks. Report results per scenario including failures, model/provider/version and exact code revision. The recorded 12-case corpus is a useful start, not evidence of complete clinical validation.</p>
$(New-ShotSlot '11' 'Agent evaluation results' 'Insert an actual golden-case/pytest report showing expected versus actual outcomes and prompt-injection/safe-failure cases.')

<h1>19. Performance Evaluation</h1>$performanceBody
<p>Performance results are not present in the reviewed completion plan. Run and report measurements; do not populate the template with estimates. Measure normal CRUD/API and agent latency separately because model/provider behavior can dominate the end-to-end time.</p>
<table><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Measured result</th><th>Required context</th></tr><tr><td>API p50 / p95 / p99</td><td>[RUN AND ENTER]</td><td>Commit, deployment/environment, endpoint, concurrency and sample size.</td></tr><tr><td>PostgreSQL query/transaction p95</td><td>[RUN AND ENTER]</td><td>Dataset size, indexes, PostgreSQL version and connection settings.</td></tr><tr><td>Agent workflow p50 / p95 and fallback rate</td><td>[RUN AND ENTER]</td><td>Provider/model/version, timeout, concurrency and scenario corpus.</td></tr><tr><td>Throughput / error rate</td><td>[RUN AND ENTER]</td><td>Load profile, duration, hardware/resources and error breakdown.</td></tr><tr><td>Notification enqueue/delivery latency</td><td>[RUN AND ENTER]</td><td>Provider/device, retry policy and what counts as delivery.</td></tr></table>
$(New-ShotSlot '12' 'Performance charts' 'Insert genuine load-test output with p50/p95/p99, throughput and errors clearly labeled with test environment and commit.')

<h1>20. CI/CD &amp; Git Workflow</h1>
<h2>20.1 Continuous integration pipelines</h2><table><tr><th>Pipeline</th><th>Recorded activities</th><th>Evidence expected</th></tr><tr><td>Backend CI</td><td>Restore/build/test .NET solution using PostgreSQL service; generate idempotent EF migration SQL artifact.</td><td>Passing run linked to submission SHA; test log and migration artifact.</td></tr><tr><td>Agent CI</td><td>Python environment, Ruff lint, pytest agent tests.</td><td>Passing lint/tests and scenario report.</td></tr><tr><td>React CI</td><td>npm ci, production build and Vitest.</td><td>Passing run and build artifact.</td></tr><tr><td>Flutter CI</td><td>Flutter setup, pub get, analyze, tests and release APK build artifact.</td><td>Analyze/test run; APK artifact and install verification.</td></tr><tr><td>Container / integration CI</td><td>Compose config/build and Flutter-to-agent-to-React integration workflow with evidence artifact.</td><td>Actual successful stack run and redacted audit JSON/log artifacts.</td></tr></table>
<h2>20.2 Collaboration and contribution traceability</h2><p>Assignment expectations include meaningful commits, branches, issues, pull requests, reviews, conflict resolution and a project board. CI files exist, but repository configuration alone does not prove that each pipeline passed or that each member contributed regularly. Attach repository URL, representative reviewed PRs, issue ownership, commit links for all four members and a concise conflict-resolution example if applicable. Never back-fill or manufacture Git evidence.</p>
