<h1>22. Architecture Decision Records</h1>
<p>The repository contains six accepted ADRs, dated August 2026. The records are the primary written evidence for LO4 and should be included in full or appended to the final consolidated PDF.</p>
<table><tr><th>ADR</th><th>Decision</th><th>Rationale and consequence</th></tr><tr><td>01 — Domain and component assignment</td><td>Four student-owned domains map to donor, request, inventory and camp/notification responsibilities, each with a distinct agent.</td><td>Clear ownership and viva boundaries; names must be mapped and evidence linked.</td></tr><tr><td>02 — React state management</td><td>React Context for authentication and TanStack Query for server state; local state for filters/selections.</td><td>Cache/invalidation matches API-owned data and avoids unnecessary global state.</td></tr><tr><td>03 — Flutter state management</td><td>Riverpod, typed HTTP service and flutter_secure_storage for refresh tokens.</td><td>Testable state and protected long-lived credential storage; physical-device verification remains necessary.</td></tr><tr><td>04 — Agent framework and orchestration</td><td>Fixed LangGraph coordinator → analysis → dispatch → validation flow; optional Ollama with deterministic fallback.</td><td>Inspectable bounded delegation; model cannot authorize side effects.</td></tr><tr><td>05 — Agent workflow data strategy</td><td>API-owned relational workflow/step/approval records plus versioned structured JSON payload fields.</td><td>Queryable audit state while payloads can evolve; durable graph checkpoint/recovery remains an open gap.</td></tr><tr><td>06 — Cloud deployment</td><td>Vercel web, Render API/agent and Neon PostgreSQL; Docker Compose locally; Azure for Students fallback.</td><td>No-cost evaluator access targeted; actual account, uptime, backups and URLs still need verification.</td></tr></table>
<p>For each ADR, include Context, Options Considered, Decision and Consequences. Keep the original one-page ADR files consistent with the final topology and implementation.</p>

<h1>23. Challenges / Limitations</h1>$($sectionBodies[13])
<h2>23.1 Research and operational limitations</h2><p>There is no evidence in the reviewed repository of stakeholder interviews or a validated workflow study. The NBTS already documents systems for blood-bank management, stock monitoring and donor appointments; therefore LifeLink’s intended role should be tested as an additive coordination concept with relevant authority, not positioned as a substitute. No actual measurement proves reduced response time, reduced wastage or increased donor availability.</p>
<p>Other key limitations recorded by the project include missing real-PostgreSQL race/rollback testing, durable agent checkpoint/retry semantics, unfinished client workflows, no measured performance report, outstanding security/privacy scans and reviews, missing production deployment evidence, and unverified physical Android release behavior. Clinical business rules have not been shown to be professionally validated. No live deployment, evaluator URL, APK installation result or access period should be claimed without current evidence.</p>
<h2>23.2 Screenshot and evidence placement guide</h2><table><tr><th>Report section</th><th>Recommended evidence image</th><th>Evidence quality rule</th></tr><tr><td>5–6</td><td>Requirements/roles and domain component overview.</td><td>Keep role names and student ownership consistent with source and project board.</td></tr><tr><td>8–10</td><td>System architecture and EER are already editable diagrams; add schema/migration evidence.</td><td>Use current data model and synthetic records.</td></tr><tr><td>11–12</td><td>React admin and Flutter user journeys.</td><td>Capture current build, meaningful state and role; no real personal data.</td></tr><tr><td>13–18</td><td>Agent execution trace, approval, tests and golden scenario results.</td><td>Show request/correlation IDs consistently and redact payloads.</td></tr><tr><td>19–21</td><td>Performance charts, GitHub Actions, deployment health and APK.</td><td>Include run date, commit, environment and artifact source; no fabricated values.</td></tr></table>

